<span><span><span><span>Hop City</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Collab)</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/5907b580-202f-7631-9f30-1b6cc809e943.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍻 Can’t get enough Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Grimm Festooning</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Zero Gravity Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/08d0c476-c85c-f266-823d-97bbf4081333.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f47b/72.png\" alt=\"👻\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> Boo! </span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Blue Mountain Spooky</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Barrel Aged Pumpkin Ale with cocoa nibs</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span>Union Craft Fest</span></span></strong><span><span> Festbier</span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/586bf1e5-f988-8903-bd34-9d8bee8cbb96.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🫶 Covet the </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Coven</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hops<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>DDH Through the Abyss</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Motueka &amp; Rakau<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Sailing on the Rings of Saturn</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy DIPA with Citra, Galaxy, Nelson Sauvin &amp; Motueka<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Hidden Realm </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Hazy IPA with Citra, Nelson Sauvin &amp; Rakau</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/3310afa2-b4f8-cdb4-86a7-0a7be85e3415.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍂 Seasonal Bliss<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>First State Autumn Bliss</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pumpkin Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>First State Brewery Gnome </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Oktoberfest Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Live Oak Oaktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/0a940c28-de79-750b-0045-c73f03cd5766.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🧮 4 x </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Threes</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> = Beer<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Hereafter </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Festbier<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Vliet</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> German Pilsner<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Logical Conclusion </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>IPA with Citra, Simcoe &amp; Mosaic<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Then, Suddenly</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with 100% Cryo Hops</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/5a45aeab-a355-4a90-e333-e6ae1cbf8a39.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍺 Built to drink with</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Foam</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Built To Spill</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> NE DIPA with Galaxy &amp; Citra<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Dead Wax</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> IPA with Denali, Vic Secret &amp; Azacca</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/28497daa-cd82-aaa7-2e17-583b97d658c8.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><strong><span>Prost Packs</span></strong><span>! #1 includes one of each: </span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span><span>Bingo Beer Oktoberfest, Star Hill Festie, Rhinegeist Franz, Sierra Nevada Oktoberfest, Victory Festbier</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> &amp;</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Aslin Festbier</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>!</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Maine Beer Prince Percy Pilsner</p>\n<p>Brainstorm Psych Eval Hazy DIPA</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/18a6f1b9-4503-309d-0f51-d982632f6b28.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Sophie Schaal NV Cremant d'Alsace Extra Brut</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>I have a little wine crush on Sophie Schaal. Born and raised in Burgundy, Sophie has now rooted herself in my favorite wine region of Alsace, where she is crafting swoon-worthy wines including this new sparkler that has been described as an eleven out of ten. Bone dry and pristine with green apple, lemon zest, white flowers, and a subtle hint of brioche and almond. Hand Harvested &amp; Organic.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Giacomo Borgogno Dolcetto d'Alba</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Giacomo Borgogno &amp; Figli is considered a dynasty of Barolo, founded in 1761 and boasting underground cellars that represent a rare living historical memory of the Langhe. And if Barolo is King, Dolcetto is the fun, easy-going cousin. Perfect to pair with your favorite cheese board. Dark cherries, wild herbs and soft and delicate tannins. Organic &amp; Native Yeast.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span>Tinazzi Valpolicella Ripasso Superiore</span></span><span><span>: </span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Hello rich, big Italian wine. If you're not familiar with the Ripasso method (Italian for \"re-do it\"), consider it your baby Amarone. Leftover grapes and skins from big brother, Amarone, macerate with the Valpolicella for a turbo boost of richness, body, and complexity. Ripe cherries, dried plums, vanilla, tobacco, and cocoa with a whisper of licorice and oak.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/17be8c45-a31c-5796-33cd-97289371759c.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span>Coming Out of My Cage and I’ve Been Doing Just Wine</span></p>\n<p><span>For a lot of folks, the tail end of August heralds the beginning of fall—think Oktoberfest beers, back-to-school shopping, and all things pumpkin spice. Me? I prefer to hang on to summer with a white-knuckle grip. But on those days where there’s a cool breeze in the air and an Albariño or a Sauvignon Blanc just aren’t cutting it, I’m reaching for something with a little more body and a whole lot of character. </span></p>\n<p><span>Enter </span><strong><span>Mr. Brightside’s Gamay Noir</span></strong><span>. This smooth, ruby-red stunner from winemaker Tim Fulnecky is just as gorgeous in the glass as it is on the palate. Derived entirely from grapes grown in the Zabala vineyard in Arroyo Seco, it’s cold-soaked for three days before being spontaneously fermented and pressed to stainless steel. Aging in French Oak slowly introduces a subtle level of earthy tannins while hanging on to the wine’s natural bright, acidic charm. The result is a light, jammy, silky sip with punches of raspberry, strawberry, and violets.</span></p>\n<p><span>This Gamay is perfectly fine straight out the bottle, but also benefits from a quick chill. Pair with herby roasted chicken, rich prosciutto and brie, a beet salad, or a hearty mushroom&nbsp;pasta. Cheers!</span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Erika</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ee114eb5-8f0d-9c75-610a-7cf185e13f8a.png\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
